Type a pod-backed value into a web form field without seeing the value yourself.
You supply the field's accessibility-snapshot `ref` (from web_modal_scan) plus a `pod_id` and `projection`. The tool resolves the value at courier scope and types it via Playwright; the tool result reports only that the field was filled and how many characters were typed — never the value itself.
Use for sensitive fields whose value lives in an identity pod (SSN, account numbers, full DOB). For non-sensitive fields with known values, use `browser_type` or `web_type_focused` with the literal text instead.
Do not call `pod_fetch` to retrieve the value and then type it via another tool — that defeats the privacy boundary and leaks the value into your transcript.
